# scoursh scope - rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.4
#
# REQUIRED for `dast`.  The single most important safety control in the tool:
# DAST refuses any host absent from here and there is no raw-URL bypass.
# `sast`, `sca` and `iac` do not need this file at all
# (docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 14).
#
# The gate matches a normalised (scheme, host, port) tuple.  Path is NOT part of
# the gate; it bounds the crawler's frontier, which is a coverage control rather
# than a safety one (docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 19).

id: example-target
base-url: https://target.example/app
allow-subdomains: false
allow-private-addresses: false
tls-expect-wildcard: false
notes: tls-expect-wildcard declares that a wildcard certificate is the
  INTENDED design for this target, so modules/dast/passive/tls.sh does not
  report one. Leave it false for a host-specific service. It is per target,
  not scanner-wide, because an estate legitimately has both shapes and one
  global answer would make a false positive indistinguishable from a real
  finding. Free text, safely. A pipe | a colon: a hash # and a "quote" are all
  ordinary bytes here, which is the whole reason config/scope.conf uses the
  block-record format instead of `name | base_url | notes`.
